@subsection date.h

@defun formatDate (CString str, int dfmt, int mfmt, int yfmt, int sfmt, bool cmplx) @arrow{} String
The arguments @code{dfmt} @code{mfmt} @code{yfmt} @code{sfmt}
@code{cmplx} say how to format the different parts of string @code{str} containing a
date.

The argument @code{dfmt} says how to format the day @code{day} part of the date..
@itemize @bullet
@item 0
number, with a leading space for single digits
@item 1
number, with a leading zero for single digits
@item 2
number as is, no leading space, no leading zero
@end itemize
The argument @code{mfmt}, says how to format the @code{month} part of the date..
@itemize @bullet
@item 0
month number, with a leading space for single digits
@item 1
month number, with a leading zero for single digits
@item 2
month number, as is, no leading space, no leading zero
@item 3
month name, three letter abbreviation, all capitals
@item 4
month name, three letter abbreviation, first letter capitalized
@item 5
month name, spelled out, all capitals
@item 6
month name, spelled out, first letter capitalize
@end itemize

The argument @code{yfmt}, says how to tofmrat the @code{year} part of the date.
Currently, no formats are specified and it is ignored.

The argument @code{sfmt}, says how to arrange the @code{day},
@code{month}, and @code{year} pieces.

@itemize @bullet
@item 0
@code{day} @code{month} @code{year}
@item 1
@code{month} @code{day} @code{year}
@item 2
@code{month}/@code{day}/@code{year}
@item 3
@code{day}/@code{month}/@code{year}
@item 4
@code{month}-@code{day}-@code{year}
@item 5
@code{day}-@code{month}-@code{year}
@item 6
@code{month} @code{day} @code{year} with no spaces
@item 7
@code{day} @code{month} @code{year} with no spaces
@item 8
@code{year} @code{month} @code{day}
@item 9
@code{year}/@code{month}/@code{day}
@item 10
@code{year}-@code{month}-@code{day}
@item 11
@code{year} @code{month} @code{day} with no spaces
@end itemize

The argument @code{cmplx}, a boolean, if @code{true}, says to treat
the string @code{str} as a complex date, including date modifiers,
ranges, and/or double-dating.
@end defun

@defun extractDate (CString string, int* pmod, int* pday, int* pmonth, int* pyear, String* pystr) @arrow{} void
Attempt to extract date from any string.
@end defun

